" Vim will error when it encounters overloading a function name
"/   WORKAROUND: reserved exclamation mark
" 		Situaton: colision of exclamation marked functions
" 			Vim over writes with new information as it comes in
"				so, the lastly declared instance get used

" BEST PRECTICE
"				ALWAYS USE ABORT and use try catch 

function DeAmp () range
	echo 'DeAmping lines '.a:firstline.' to '.a:lastline
	execute a:firstline.','.a:lastline.'s/&/&amp;/g'
endfunction
" key word range in the function signature 
" this tells the function to capture the range variable
" meaning this function can use 2 extra builtin variables
		"  a:firstline
		"	 a:lastline
		" these are of type string but are references to line numbers

" Maps and functions
function! DeAmp(line)
	if a:lines > 1 
		echo 'DeAmping '.a:lines.' lines'
	endif
	execute '.,+'.(a:lines-1).'s/&/&amp;/ge'
endfunction

map <silent> && :<C-U>call DeAmp(v:count1)<CR>
" <silent> surpress errors messages
" if the mapping activation charaters '&&' had a number infront of it
" to signify how many times to do this. this number is held in the
" builin reserved v:count1. If not given, default is 1

" the :<C-U> control uppercase U
"		clears all line range information associated with this sequence
" Expanding upon what <C-U> does...
" 	Situation: 4&&  is excuted as defined above. this will be expanded as
"		:.,+3<C-U>call DeAmp(4)<CR>
"		and then the <C-U> will cancel out the range info right before it
